uperior deep margin  which is the  closest margin of approach  This tumor is representatively sampled as FSA and  sampled for flow cytometry and ER PR studies  Tumor was also given to Dr   Eberlein s laboratory for special studies  The specimen is inked blue on the  lateral superior half  black on the medial superior half  yellow on the  inferior medial half  and green on the lateral inferior half  Tumor is 2 5cm  from the skin ellipse   Micro 1  FSRA and tumor in relation to closest margin  2 frag  1 cass   Micro 2  Tumor in relation to deep margin  RSS  1 frag  1 cass   Micro 3  Tumor in relation to superior margin  RSS  1 frag  1 cass   Micro 4  Tumor in relation to inferior margin  RSS  1 frag  1 cass   Micro 5  Tumor in relation to lateral margin  RSS  1 frag  1 cass   Micro 6  Medial margin  RSS  2 frag  1 cass   Micro 7  Skin and subjacent tissue  RSS  1 frag  1 cass   Micro 8  Tumor and deep margin  RSS  1 frag  1 cass   The second part of the specimen  labeled  axillary contents   consists of a REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm fragment of yellow red  adipose tissue containing one  1  lymph  node  which is very firm and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm  with areas of yellow  necrosis  There are multiple  smaller  grossly involved  and uninvolved lymph  nodes  Half of the largest grossly involved lymph node was given to Dr   Eberlein s laboratory for special studies  There are seventeen  17  possible  lymph nodes identified  ranging up to 3 2cm in maximal dimension   Micro REMOVED_DATE  Possible lymph nodes  RSS  multi frag  5 cass   ahv  Reports to  EBERLEIN  TIMOTHY  JOSEPH M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  LUMPECTOMY  ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  AXILLARY NODES   report_end  , not_surgery.
