Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  KRANE  JEFFREY  FRED  M D  PH D   DIAGNOSIS  by KRANE JEFFREY FRED M D  PH D   LEFT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   Florid epithelial hyperplasia   Multifocal fibroadenomatous change   Sclerosing adenosis   Prior biopsy site   Cysts   Apocrine metaplasia   Microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium   Skin with cicatrix   Seborrheic keratosis   Skeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change   No residual invasive or in situ carcinoma identified   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 41 yo female s p REMOVED_DATE L breast conserving surgery with excision of  2 masses revealing 0 5cm mixed ductal   lobular invasive carcinoma   DCIS   DCIS 2 negative sentinel nodes  Pt has completed adjuvant AC  chemotherapy   Operation  Left simple mastectomy with tissue expander   Clinical Diagnosis  L breast cancer   TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Left breast  short suture superior  long suture axillary  tail   GROSS DESCRIPTION  by YOU MINGJIAN JAMES M D  PH D   The specimen is received fresh in one part   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and  unit number  The specimen is a 420 gram  left simple mastectomy breast tissue  with tissue expander  17 x 13 x 2 4cm   with a white tan skin ellipse  7 5 x  3 3cm   and an attached axillary tail  2 5 x 2 x 1 0cm    There is a 2 5cm   linear well healed surgical scar in the lower outer quadrant  1 2cm from the  unremarkable 0 5cm nipple  A firm white area  2 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm   is  1cm deep to this area and represents possible healed scar tissue  The deep  margin is a smooth fascial plane with an attached skeletal muscle  1 0 x REMOVED_DATE x  0 2cm   which is 2 7cm from the lateral and 2 7cm from the superior areas of  the specimen  The deep margin is inked black and the muscle is inked blue   There is a red tan solid nodule  0 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm   located 0 5cm from the  lateral tip of the left skin tissue  The breast consists of approximately 60   of yellow tan adipose tissue and approximately 40  of white tan fibrous  tissue  One cystic lesion is identified in the upper outer quadrant  0 6cm  from the deep margin  and measures 0 4cm in diameter  Two white tan  solid  nodules are identified  One is located 0 5cm from the deep margin  2cm from  the medial scar and is located in the lower outer quadrant  A second nodule   0 3cm in diameter  is located 1 2cm from the deep margin  and is 2cm from  the previous excision site  The second nodule is located in the lower outer  quadrant  The two nodules are approximately 1 5cm apart  Six possible lymph  nodes are identified in the axillary tail  the largest measuring 0 8cm in  greatest dimension and entirely submitted   Micro 1  previous excision site  1 frag  ESS   Micro 2  cystic lesion of breast  1 frag  RSS   Micro 3  first nodule of the breast  1 frag  ESS   Micro 4  second nodule of the breast  1 frag  ESS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE  additional breast tissue close to the previous excision  site  11 frags  RSS   Micro 7  upper outer quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro 8  upper inner quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro 9  lower outer quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro 10  lower inner quadrant  1 frag  RSS   Micro 11  skeletal muscle  1 frag  ESS   Micro 12  skin lesion  2 frags  ESS   Micro 13  nipple and surrounding tissue  1 frag  RSS   Micro 14  representative section of skin scar  1 frag  RSS   Micro REMOVED_DATE  6 possible lymph nodes  ESS   mjy  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D   SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE   report_end  , Mastectomy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 39 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    WITH A MUCINOUS COMPONENT  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 1 HIGH POWER FIELD FROM THE DEEP MARGIN AND AN ADDITIONAL MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   5    LOW GRADE  3  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  ALL 8 LYMPH NODES DISPLAY PROMINENT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION  4  MONCKEBERG S MEDIAL CALCIFIC SCLEROSIS  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progestrogne receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast tissue  is a left modified radical mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm skin ellipse containing a central 2 5cm unremarkable nipple  No definite scar is identified  Attached to the specimen is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm firm  stellate tan mass that focally extends to within less than 1 0mm of the deep resection margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Section Code  A  mass with deep resection margin  representative section  B E  mass  representative sections  F  nipple trisected in entirety  G  unremarkable parenchyma  representative sections  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal a 2 5cm focus of matted lymph nodes with a homogenous tan cut surface  Further sectioning reveals several firm lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  All have a homogeneous tan cut surface  Representative sections of the lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes H through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
