Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  29 AUG 94 at 12 58 CLINICAL DATA  69 year old female with a right axillary node  measuring 3 0cm that was positive for cancer consistent with metastatic breast carcinoma at an outside hospital  Admitted for a modified radical mastectomy  Palpable right periareolar mass biopsy and frozen for second mass today      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL TISSUE RECEIVED Revised by  Shane Meehan  MD Revised on 01 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 37                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY AND MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND PAPILLOMATOSIS  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The carcinoma is multifocal  but involvement extends to 1 5cm in greatest dimension as measured on the slide section  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  The resection margins and 19 of 19 lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  No vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  70    POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  30    NOTE  The tumor is approximately 1 0cm in maximum dimension  The resection margins and 9 of 9 lymph nodes are free of carcinoma  The intraductal component is predominantly of the cribriform type  No vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MASS    THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface with some focal firm areas measuring 0 8cm in greatest dimension  Representative section frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remaining tissue submitted entirely in A through H  Received in three containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Labeled  Additional left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue  Three ly