Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 10 CLINICAL DATA  51 year old female with left breast mass    primary breast carcinoma vs  metastatic gastric carcinoma                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSIES  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA  NOTE  The tumor cells infiltrate in cords and small nests and contain slight to moderate amounts of eosinophilic to slightly basophilic cytoplasm and hyperchromatic nuclei  Occasional signet rings cells are present  Histologically  the features are consistent with invasive lobular carcinoma  In addition  an immunoperoxidase stain for gross cystic disease fluid protein  GCDFP   often positive in breast adenocarcinoma  is also focally positive in this case  The slides from the previous gastric carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   were not available for review  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 51     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 12 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is an aggregate of soft  tan pink fragments of membranous  fibrofatty tissue measuring 2 x 2 x 0 2cm  submitted entirely in cassette A  Gross Description by  Jason Corbin Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Rachana Jain  M D  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSIES , not_surgery.
