 REMOVED_CASE_ID  SIMON ROSE R 80 F  REG REF 05 26    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC PANISZYN LUCY M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  05 26 05  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  History of left breast carcinoma diagnosed REMOVED_DATE  treated at DFCI  diagnosed at B W  new suspicious microcalcifications upper outer quadrant right breast  ductal carcinoma in situ vs  fibrocystic changes Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereotactic breast biopsy  right breast calcifications  and is contained in a purple cassette  The specimen consists of three firm  yellowish tan needle biopsies ranging in size from 1 8cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter to 2 3cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter  Submitted in cassette 1  3X all  Also present in the container is a 3 x 3 x 0 4cm  aggregate of yellowish pink  firm needle biopsies admixed with blood clot each measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  Submitted in cassettes   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  agg  all  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  upper outer quadrant  needle biopsy  Atypical ductal hyperplasia  columnar cell type  with microcalcifications  Ductal hyperplasia  fibrocystic changes  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  The previous left breast needle biopsy   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   has been reviewed  The current case has been reviewed by Dr  Frederick Koerner  of the Massachusetts General Hospital  who concurs with the diagnosis  He comments   A small duct and several associated terminal duct lobular units in this core biopsy specimen harbor atypical ductal cells of the columnar type  They appear enlarged and they possess slightly enlarged  smoothly contoured  oval nuclei  homogeneous chromatin  inconspicuous nucleoli  and abundant  apical cytoplasm  These cytological features indicate the presence of atypicality  but the cells do not display significant architectural atypism  They grow in a crowded  single layer without piling up  Because of the presence of cytological atypia without architectural atypia  I would make the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar cell type  Ordinarily  I regard this finding as an indication for an excision  however  the age of the patient and the presence of a contralateral carcinoma make me question the need for further surgery in the case at hand   Final Diagnosis by  Michael J  Ross  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD ROSMJ Notes  REMOVED_DATE  Two slides ret d  jam  CR  REMOVED_DATE  Rec d MGH path report from Dr  Koerner via fax  dg REMOVED_DATE  Sent two slides  1 1L and 3L  to Dr  Frederick Koerner   MGH via courier for opinion MJR jam  CO   617  REMOVED_DATE Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Right breast  N Atypical hyperp  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Columnar epithe BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Intraductal hyp BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Fibrocystic dis Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILDCOPIES TO  PANISZYN LUCY M D   REMOVED_CASE_ID  WASHINGTON ST   SUITE 546 NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 964  REMOVED_CASE_ID  RUBENS JAMI R  M D  RADIOLOGY DEPARTMENT NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID ICD CODES  REMOVED_DATE   Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILDMARKERS  Breast Disease Related  Consult Case Out  Consult Case Return Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORDPROCEDURES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   06 01 0