Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  37   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  MGH Pathology  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 15 39  Results To   Jennifer A Shin MD  E Tessa Hedley Whyte MD  MB    CLINICAL HISTORY   Breast Adenocarcinoma Metastatic to Brain Central Nervous System  Cerebellum     SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     GROSS DESCRIPTION   1 block s  from Massachusetts General Hospital  the archived specimen was  retrieved and reviewed for adequacy    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID               TEST    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST  Breast Adenocarcinoma Metastatic to Brain Central Nervous  System  Cerebellum     SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     RESULTS     Fibroblast Growth Factor Receptor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   copy number analysis      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Reference Probe Copy Number Ratio  REMOVED_DATE    INTERPRETATION     The FISH data are consistent with NO amplification of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene     TEST INFORMATION   Aberrations involving the fibroblast growth factor receptor 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   gene have  been noted in tumors of multiple types  including certain lung  breast  ovarian   skeletal muscle  melanocytic and hematopoietic neoplasms   1  Amplification of  the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene was recently identified as a significant and common finding  22   by FISH  in a cohort of squamous cell carcinomas of the lung   2     The assay performed on this patient uses fluorescence in situ hybridization   FISH  on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor specimens to analyze  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene  amplification status  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A  dual color FISH assay was performed using Bacterial Artificial Chromosome probe  CTD  REMOVED_CASE_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   chromosome 8p   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus  home brew  and a copy number probe   centromere 8  Abbott Vysis 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  or 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       Signal quantitation was used to generate a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  centromere 8 ratio   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  Centromere 8 ratios are interpreted as follows  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered  borderline for amplification  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification   and greater than REMOVED_DATE or clustered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  signals that are too numerous to count  would be considered highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     REFERENCES   1  Turner N and Grose R  Fibroblast growth factor signaling  from  development to cancer  Nature Reviews Cancer 10 116   REMOVED_CASE_ID     2  Weiss J  Sos  M  et al  Frequent and focal  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  amplification  associates with therapeutically tractable  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  dependency in squamous cell lung  cancer  Sci Transl Med 2 62  62ra93   REMOVED_CASE_ID       This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Center for Integrated Diagnostics   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Jackson  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Valentina Nardi MD         PART   Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID        report_end  , Excisional_biopsy_(Lumpectomy).
