ATE x 1 2cm   unoriented  irregular shaped portion of breast tissue  One portion of the  specimen is slightly granular and the other is more convex  The convex surface  is presumed to be the true margin of this specimen and is inked entirely black   Serial sections reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  well circumscribed  soft white  area in the mid portion of the specimen  The entire specimen is submitted in  six cassettes  6 agg  all   SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    remainder of the specimen  Specimen C is received in formalin  labeled  left breast  3   designated as the   most inferior margin  and consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm   irregular shaped portion of breast tissue  The entire specimen is inked black   The specimen is serially sectioned and no abnormalities are seen  The specimen  is entirely submitted in two cassettes  labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4X all   Specimen D is received in formalin  labeled  left breast final margins  and  consists of multiple small  irregular shaped fragments of soft  yellow  tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  in aggregate dimension  The entire  specimen is submitted in four cassettes  labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 agg  all   Specimen E is received fresh  labeled  left axillary node contents  and  consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  portion of adipose tissue with multiple   palpable lymph nodes  The fat is dissected revealing seventeen lymph  nodes  Eight of the smaller lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm   to 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  Nine of the larger lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE x 1  x 0 5cm  to REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 2cm  The largest lymph node  on serially sectioning   reveals a white  firm cut surface consistent with tumor   SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    lymph nodes  not bisected   16X all    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    serially sectioned largest lymph node 