epithelial layer in areas of invasive carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  An immunostain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  was performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and highlights endothelial cells  An immunostain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is non contributory  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast mastectomy   is a 30 x 18 x 4 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a 28 x 13cm overlying skin ellipse with a 4 x 3cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The skin is white and the specimen is oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The anterior surface is inked blue and posterior surface is inked black and specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm firm tan ill demarcated centrally hemorrhagic mass which is 1 5cm from the closest posterior resection margin and 3cm from the closest anterior resection margin  The mass is located in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen  There is also a separate REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 7cm fibrotic area 4cm from the first mass  and located approximately in the midline of the specimen  The area of fibrosis is 5cm from the posterior resection margin and 3cm from the anterior resection margin and skin ellipse  The rest of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative section is submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior resection margin to the 1st mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest anterior margin to the 1st mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the 1st mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the described fibrotic area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior resection to the 2nd mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of the nipple  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 03   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 30 32PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  Focally  the tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells    Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells    Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 08   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 20 04AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HY